        <li><strong>Enter Mortgage Terms</strong> — Add your interest rate and loan term. At <%= currentYear %> rates of 7–7.5%, leverage significantly impacts your CoC return. Use our <a href="<%= baseUrl %>/loan-calculators/mortgage-calculator">mortgage calculator</a> to explore different scenarios.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter Rental Income</strong> — Input monthly rent and vacancy rate. The <strong>1% rule</strong> says rent should be ≥1% of purchase price for positive cash flow.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter Operating Expenses</strong> — Include property tax, insurance, maintenance (use the 1% rule: 1% of property value annually), management fees, and HOA costs.</li>
        <li><strong>Review Results</strong> — See your CoC return, NOI, cap rate, monthly cash flow, and a benchmark comparison. A <strong>good CoC return is 8–12%</strong> in 2026.</li>
